      "name": "service_sentiment",
      "causal_role": "treatment",
      "named_in_query": false,
      "rationale": "Service quality is an intervenable lever a business can actually improve; its measured sentiment stands in as the treatment on the service dimension."
    },
    {
      "name": "food_sentiment",
      "causal_role": "treatment",
      "named_in_query": false,
      "rationale": "Food quality is a configurable operational property a business can change; treated here as an intervenable treatment dimension."
    },
    {
      "name": "value_sentiment",
      "causal_role": "treatment",
      "named_in_query": false,
      "rationale": "Pricing/value is a settable business decision, hence an intervenable treatment lever."
    },
    {
      "name": "ambiance_sentiment",
      "causal_role": "treatment",
      "named_in_query": false,
      "rationale": "Ambiance is something a business can deliberately alter (decor, lighting, layout); an intervenable lever."
    },
    {
      "name": "primary_complaint",
      "causal_role": "mediator",
      "named_in_query": false,
      "rationale": "A summary of what drove dissatisfaction; it is downstream of the underlying dimensions and reflects the outcome perception rather than a common cause of treatment and outcome."
    },
    {
      "name": "top_positive_driver",
      "causal_role": "mediator",
      "named_in_query": false,
      "rationale": "A derived attribution of which dimension produced positive perception; sits on the causal path to satisfaction, not an adjusting confounder."
    },
    {
      "name": "satisfaction_driver",
      "causal_role": "mediator",
      "named_in_query": false,
      "rationale": "Combines strength/weakness attribution; a summary along the path to satisfaction, not a common cause of the levers and the outcome."
    }
  ],
  "treatment_present": true,
  "treatment_columns": ["service_sentiment", "food_sentiment", "value_sentiment", "ambiance_sentiment"],
  "treatment_intervenable": true,
  "confounders": [],
  "confounder_quality": 0.0,
  "rationale": "The added columns supply plausible intervenable treatment dimensions (service, food, value, ambiance) that a business could actually set or change, satisfying part (a) of the claim. However, the schema contains NO confounders: nothing adjusts for common causes of both a dimension's quality and overall satisfaction (e.g., customer expectations, price tier/segment, location, cuisine type, time/occasion, reviewer strictness). The remaining aspect/driver columns are attribution mediators along the causal path, not confounders, and cannot be used to identify a counterfactual effect. Because part (b) is entirely unmet, the interventional (what-if) claim is not realized."
}
